{"step_index":1389,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T17:26:47Z","content":"### ⚡ Swipe-to-Dial & Swipe-to-Skip Gesture Enhancements\n\n### Root Cause\nPreviously, `onStartShouldSetPanResponder` was set to `true`, which caused the gesture handler to intercept raw button taps and vertical scrolling, while the horizontal release threshold (`120px`) was too wide for a quick, natural thumb swipe.\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ What Has Been Implemented ([`DialerHudScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx))\n\n1. **Direction-Aware Gesture Recognition:**\n   - Gestures now activate strictly on horizontal swipes (`|dx| > 8px` and `|dx| > |dy|`), allowing vertical scrolling and button taps inside the card to work seamlessly without interference.\n\n2. **Snappy & Responsive Thresholds:**\n   - Swiping threshold reduced to **70px** or flick velocity **`vx > 0.4`**.\n   - **Swipe Right ➔**: Triggers native dialer (`tel:`) immediately with smooth haptic feedback.\n   - **Swipe Left ➔**: Advances to the next educator immediately.\n\n3. **Fluid Card Physics & Dynamic Feedback Banner:**\n   - Added subtle interactive card rotation (`-6°` to `+6°`) as you drag.\n   - **Dynamic Floating Pill Banner**:\n     - Pulling right illuminates **`📞 RELEASE TO DIAL`** in emerald green (`#10B981`).\n     - Pulling left illuminates **`⏭️ RELEASE TO SKIP`** in amber (`#F59E0B`).\n   - Smooth spring snapback if released before crossing the threshold.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Production Deployment Live\nThe updated gesture build is compiled and published live:\n👉 **[https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh](https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh)**"}
