{"step_index":1397,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T17:27:26Z","thinking":"**Defining Interest Length**\n\nRight now, I'm focused on how to handle the length of interests displayed on report cards. I'm thinking of examples like guaranteed bonuses, comparing pension options, and calculating timelines. These interests can vary in length, so I'm figuring out how they will best render in the `interestChip` container, specifically looking at how the `flexDirection` and `alignItems` properties come into play.\n\n\n**Refining Interest Display**\n\nI've determined that long interests will break the screen layout without text wrapping and `maxWidth: '100%'`. My focus has shifted to making \"Report Card Needs & Inquiries\" wrap cleanly. I'm exploring 